From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [EXPERIMENT] ASoC: q6asm-dai: tell the DSP to run before queueing writes

On this target the ADSP acknowledges every command it is given, including
the AFE port start and the stream open, and then never returns a single
WRITE_DONE. Tracing what actually goes out over APR shows the writes
leaving before the session is ever told to run:

	ASM_STREAM_CMD_OPEN_WRITE_V3
	ASM_DATA_CMD_MEDIA_FMT_UPDATE_V2
	ASM_DATA_CMD_WRITE_V2  token 0
	ASM_DATA_CMD_WRITE_V2  token 1
	ASM_DATA_CMD_WRITE_V2  token 2
	ASM_DATA_CMD_WRITE_V2  token 3
	ASM_SESSION_CMD_RUN_V2

That ordering is not a bug by itself, it is what the current code does
everywhere: prepare() sets the state to RUNNING, the application fills the
buffer, snd_pcm_ack() hands the periods over, and only then does ALSA
trigger the stream. It works on other Qualcomm targets, so their firmware
evidently accepts buffers while the session is stopped. This one may not,
and if it discards them there is nothing left to consume once RUN finally
arrives, which matches the observed behaviour exactly, including the fact
that how long the DSP survives scales with how much audio was queued.

So gate the queueing on RUN having been sent. The buffers the application
already wrote cannot simply be dropped, it will not write again until a
period completes, so they are queued from the trigger right after RUN.
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c	2026-08-12 22:33:49.662620009 +0000
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c	2026-08-12 22:33:49.669620009 +0000
@@ -64,6 +64,7 @@
 	unsigned int pcm_size;
 	unsigned int pcm_count;
 	unsigned int periods;
+	bool run_sent;
 	uint64_t bytes_sent;
 	uint64_t bytes_received;
 	uint64_t copied_total;
@@ -307,6 +308,8 @@
 	else
 		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING;
 
+	prtd->run_sent = false;
+
 	return ret;
 
 routing_err:
@@ -323,7 +326,8 @@
 	struct q6asm_dai_rtd *prtd = runtime->private_data;
 	int i, ret = 0, avail_periods;
 
-	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK && prtd->state == Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING) {
+	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK &&
+	    prtd->state == Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING && prtd->run_sent) {
 		avail_periods = (runtime->control->appl_ptr - prtd->queue_ptr)/runtime->period_size;
 		ASM_DIAG("ack: appl=%lu queue=%lu period=%lu avail=%d pcm_count=%u",
 			 (unsigned long)runtime->control->appl_ptr,
@@ -360,8 +364,20 @@
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_PAUSE_RELEASE:
 		ret = q6asm_run_nowait(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id,
 				       0, 0, 0);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			break;
+
+		/* Buffers may only be handed over now, and whatever the
+		 * application already wrote has to be queued here: it will not
+		 * write again until a period completes.
+		 */
+		if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK) {
+			prtd->run_sent = true;
+			ret = q6asm_dai_ack(component, substream);
+		}
 		break;
 	case SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_STOP:
+		prtd->run_sent = false;
 		ret = q6asm_cmd_nowait(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id,
 				       CMD_EOS);
 		break;
